<p><strong>Read it twice:</strong> from Bank: "one Bank administers <strong>1..*</strong> Accounts" (at least one, no upper limit); from Account: "one Account is administered by <strong>1</strong> Bank". The "one-to-many" name is just the two upper bounds: 1 on one side, many on the other.</p>
