<p>Compare with the ATM: there the whole created its parts; here the parts are created elsewhere and <strong>handed in</strong>. That single difference — <code>new</code> inside versus a parameter from outside — is the most reliable way to recognise aggregation in existing code. The program above goes further: one research center is shared by two colleges, and a department moves from one college to another without being destroyed.</p>
