<table>
<thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Class</th><th>Category</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>1</td><td>ReservationInteraction</td><td>«user interaction»</td><td>The three-step Create Reservation wizard. Collects resource, time, items, purpose and participants, shows alternatives when a slot is taken (SM-12) and the confirmation (SM-10). Contains no rule.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>ReservationCoordinator</td><td>«coordinator»</td><td>Runs the steps of UC-12 in order: validate, check the slot, save in one transaction, confirm or mark pending, create the QR token and audit entry, queue the e-mail. Keeps no state between requests.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>ReservationPolicy</td><td>«business logic»</td><td>Holds the booking rules that need other reservations or the resource: time rules BR-03…06, no overlap BR-07, approval BR-08. Answers "is this request allowed, and why not".</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>CompetencyChecker</td><td>«business logic»</td><td>Checks BR-21: a hazardous equipment item may be reserved only by a user with a valid competency for that equipment type. Reads User, Competency and Equipment.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>EmailServiceProxy</td><td>«proxy»</td><td>Local representative of the external Email Service; queues and sends confirmation mails and hides the mail protocol.</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>Reservation</td><td>«entity»</td><td>The reservation: resource, user, time range, purpose, participants and status. Answers whether it overlaps a given time range.</td></tr>
<tr><td>7</td><td>Resource, User, Competency, QRCheckInToken, AuditEntry</td><td>«entity»</td><td>Data from the static model that UC-12 reads (Resource, User, Competency) or creates (QRCheckInToken, AuditEntry).</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
